00:26:35.120 --> 00:26:37.440
And Jim immediately says, don't help him.
吉姆立刻说：别帮他。

651
00:26:37.540 --> 00:26:39.400
So no one helps him.
所以没人帮他。

652
00:26:39.540 --> 00:26:40.420
I know.
我知道。

653
00:26:40.640 --> 00:26:41.700
That is the worSt.
那真是太糟糕了。

654
00:26:41.760 --> 00:26:42.100
I know.
我知道。

655
00:26:42.200 --> 00:26:48.260
It also sets up that Pam has volunteered to make a logo for Michael's commercial.
这也为帕姆自告奋勇为迈克尔的广告设计标志做了铺垫。

656
00:26:48.480 --> 00:26:50.220
She's going to design a logo.
她要设计一个标志。

657
00:26:50.380 --> 00:26:51.160
She's very excited.
她非常兴奋。

658
00:26:51.280 --> 00:26:53.640
Well, she says she's taking an animation class.
嗯，她说她正在上动画课。

659
00:26:53.880 --> 00:26:54.760
I love that.
我喜欢这一点。

660
00:26:54.860 --> 00:26:55.280
I know.
我知道。

661
00:26:55.440 --> 00:26:56.300
I was like, go Pam.
我当时就想，加油帕姆。

662
00:26:56.680 --> 00:26:58.400
Next, the ad guys arrive.
接下来，广告公司的人到了。

663
00:26:58.800 --> 00:27:03.600
Michael runs out of the conference room, and he is immediately going to start pitching
迈克尔从会议室跑出来，立刻就开始向他们推销

664
00:27:03.600 --> 00:27:04.580
them his ideas.
他的想法。

665
00:27:04.580 --> 00:27:09.340
He says he wants this commercial to be like MTV on crack.
他说他想让这个广告看起来像嗑了药的MTV。

666
00:27:09.640 --> 00:27:10.380
He goes around.
他四处走动。

667
00:27:10.560 --> 00:27:13.140
He introduces them to everyone in the office.
他把他们介绍给办公室里的每一个人。

668
00:27:13.520 --> 00:27:15.100
There's even more in the deleted scenes.
删减片段里还有更多内容。

669
00:27:15.360 --> 00:27:21.000
He literally goes up to like every single person and does like a horrible introduction
他真的走到每个人面前，做了一次糟糕透顶的

670
00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:21.860
of all of them.
介绍。

671
00:27:21.960 --> 00:27:23.500
The way only Michael can.
只有迈克尔才做得出来。

672
00:27:23.720 --> 00:27:28.720
If you want to see some more awkward, cringey Michael introductions, go to the deleted scenes.
如果你想看更多尴尬、让人脚趾抠地的迈克尔式介绍，去看删减片段吧。

673
00:27:28.720 --> 00:27:34.480
These two ad guys were played by Kyle Bornheimer and Tim Kang.
这两个广告人分别由凯尔·博恩海默和蒂姆·康饰演。

674
00:27:34.760 --> 00:27:36.700
You probably recognize these guys.
你可能认得他们。

675
00:27:36.940 --> 00:27:39.560
Kyle has been on a ton of stuff.
凯尔演过很多作品。

676
00:27:39.560 --> 00:27:41.380
He was on Brooklyn Nine-Dine.
他演过《神烦警探》。

677
00:27:41.540 --> 00:27:43.160
He's done a bunch of commercials.
他拍过很多广告。

678
00:27:43.500 --> 00:27:44.600
Tim is the same way.
蒂姆也是一样。

679
00:27:44.800 --> 00:27:49.780
He went on to be a regular on The Mentalist and the reboot of Magnum P.I.
他后来成了《超感神探》和《夏威夷神探》重启版的主演。

680
00:27:49.780 --> 00:27:50.600
Yes.
没错。

681
00:27:50.860 --> 00:27:53.000
Are you ready for some crossover connection?
准备好迎接跨界联系了吗？

682
00:27:53.440 --> 00:27:54.540
Lay them on me.
说来听听。

683
00:27:54.880 --> 00:27:58.060
Tim, who plays Tim, ready for this?
蒂姆，就是演蒂姆的那位，准备好了吗？

684
00:27:58.280 --> 00:28:02.860
His daughter and my daughter were on the same soccer team in 2019.
他的女儿和我的女儿在2019年是同一个足球队的。

685
00:28:03.220 --> 00:28:04.320
The Falcons.
猎鹰队。

686
00:28:04.700 --> 00:28:06.280
I was the team parent.
我是球队家长代表。

687
00:28:06.480 --> 00:28:08.840
My ex-husband Warren was the coach.
我的前夫沃伦是教练。

688
00:28:09.060 --> 00:28:10.220
We make it work, y'all.
我们相处得很好，各位。

689
00:28:10.360 --> 00:28:11.200
We make it work.
我们相处得很好。

690
00:28:11.200 --> 00:28:16.320
And the Falcons made it to the finals in our AYSO division.
猎鹰队打进了我们AYSO赛区的决赛。

691
00:28:16.320 --> 00:28:19.580
We went on to play in the regional playoffs, you guys.
我们还去参加了地区季后赛，伙计们。

692
00:28:19.800 --> 00:28:22.720
And then we advanced to the area playoffs.
然后我们晋级到了区域季后赛。

693
00:28:22.940 --> 00:28:26.440
The girls came in third and they were the runner-up team to go to state.
女孩们获得了第三名，是去参加州赛的亚军队伍。

694
00:28:26.900 --> 00:28:34.720
Lady, I will never forget your messages to me during this time of Isabel's soccer team
女士，我永远不会忘记那段时间你发给我的消息，关于伊莎贝尔的足球队

695
00:28:34.720 --> 00:28:35.980
going so far.
走得那么远。

696
00:28:36.060 --> 00:28:37.700
It was the never-ending year of soccer.
那是没完没了的足球年。

697
00:28:38.020 --> 00:28:38.900
It was.
确实是。

698
00:28:38.900 --> 00:28:41.560
I would text you and I would say, what are you up to?
我会给你发短信问，你在忙什么？

699
00:28:41.640 --> 00:28:45.240
And you're like, lady, we are still in this soccer tournament.
然后你说，女士，我们还在参加这个足球锦标赛呢。

700
00:28:45.940 --> 00:28:46.280
Yes.
没错。

701
00:28:46.940 --> 00:28:48.940
But it was so exciting.
但当时真的太令人兴奋了。

702
00:28:49.100 --> 00:28:51.900
I remember how excited those girls were.
我记得那些女孩当时有多兴奋。

703
00:28:52.140 --> 00:28:55.280
And Tim is one of the other parents of another girl.
蒂姆是另一个女孩的家长之一。

704
00:28:55.460 --> 00:28:56.080
I love that.
我喜欢这一点。

705
00:28:56.340 --> 00:28:56.560
Yes.
是的。

706
00:28:57.060 --> 00:29:01.380
So Tim and I have sat on the sidelines together and cheered our girls on.
所以蒂姆和我曾一起坐在场边，为我们的女儿加油助威。

707
00:29:01.600 --> 00:29:03.260
Well, I have a connection to Kyle.
嗯，我和凯尔也有过交集。

708
00:29:03.480 --> 00:29:04.980
It's not as exciting as that.
虽然没那么令人兴奋。

709
00:29:05.120 --> 00:29:07.500
But we were both in the movie Blades of Glory.
但我们都参演了电影《冰刀双人组》。

710
00:29:07.500 --> 00:29:10.340
He played the rink PA announcer.
他扮演了溜冰场的广播员。

711
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:17.300
And so I guess in a way, we also both sat in stands and cheered on a sporting event of
所以我想在某种程度上，我们也都曾坐在看台上，为一场体育赛事加油，

712
00:29:17.300 --> 00:29:18.840
ice skating, though fictional.
也就是花样滑冰，虽然是虚构的。

713
00:29:19.140 --> 00:29:19.540
Yes.
是的。

714
00:29:19.800 --> 00:29:22.180
Well, I have another crossover connection for you, Angela.
嗯，安吉拉，我还有一个关于你们的交叉联系。

715
00:29:22.440 --> 00:29:24.040
I think I know this one.
我想我知道这个。

716
00:29:24.220 --> 00:29:25.620
This one's really weird.
这个真的很奇怪。

717
00:29:25.620 --> 00:29:28.100
And it's going to be a runner through this whole episode.
而且它会贯穿整集节目。

718
00:29:28.100 --> 00:29:36.220
Like, every guest star in this episode, Local Ad, has also had a guest appearance on Monk.
比如，这一集《本地广告》里的每一位客串明星，也都曾在《神探阿蒙》里客串过。

719
00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:38.280
It's so wild, isn't it?
太疯狂了，不是吗？

720
00:29:38.480 --> 00:29:40.180
What is going on?
这到底是怎么回事？

721
00:29:40.420 --> 00:29:46.760
Kyle played uniform cop in Mr. Monk and the Kid, and Tim played Mr. Brenneman in Mr. Monk
凯尔在《神探阿蒙与孩子》中扮演了一名制服警察，而蒂姆在《神探阿蒙》中扮演了布伦南先生，

722
00:29:46.760 --> 00:29:47.720
is up all night.
那一集叫《彻夜未眠》。

723
00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:48.500
I know.
我知道。

724
00:29:48.680 --> 00:29:49.600
It's so wild to me.
我觉得这太疯狂了。

725
00:29:49.720 --> 00:29:52.980
We have more crossover connections coming up, but there's your first two.
我们后面还有更多的交叉联系，但这是前两个。

726
00:29:52.980 --> 00:29:59.280
Now we get into this episode, and it opens with Dwight playing Second Life.
现在进入这一集，开场是德怀特在玩《第二人生》。

727
00:30:00.040 --> 00:30:07.900
And Jenna, at 3 minutes 39 seconds, is it just me, or does Dwight fly like Mother in
珍娜，在3分39秒的时候，是我多心了吗，还是德怀特飞行的姿势和《异星灾变》里的“母亲”一样？

728
00:30:07.900 --> 00:30:08.720
Raised by Wolves?
我不知道《异星灾变》这部剧。

729
00:30:09.040 --> 00:30:11.420
I don't know Raised by Wolves.
我知道。

730
00:30:11.580 --> 00:30:12.260
I know.
我就知道你会知道。

731
00:30:12.380 --> 00:30:13.320
I knew you would know it.
这听起来和《权力的游戏》很像。

732
00:30:13.320 --> 00:30:15.340
This sounds very similar to Game of Thrones.
好吧。

733
00:30:15.560 --> 00:30:15.680
Okay.
《异星灾变》和《权力的游戏》一点都不像。

734
00:30:15.880 --> 00:30:18.540
Raised by Wolves is nothing like Game of Thrones.
它简直是HBO Max上最奇怪的剧。

735
00:30:18.540 --> 00:30:23.100
It is just the weirdest show on HBO Max.
这是《异星灾变》的剧情梗概。

736
00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:25.640
Here's the overview of Raised by Wolves.
两个仿生人受命在一个神秘星球上抚养人类孩子。

737
00:30:26.140 --> 00:30:30.680
Two androids are tasked with raising human children on a mysterious planet.
当人类殖民地因宗教分歧而面临分裂时，仿生人们意识到，

738
00:30:30.680 --> 00:30:36.120
As the human colony threatens to be torn apart by religious differences, the androids learn
控制人类的信仰是一项危险且艰巨的任务。

739
00:30:36.120 --> 00:30:40.340
that controlling the beliefs of humans is treacherous and a difficult task.
而且，仿生人“母亲”还能生孩子。

740
00:30:41.220 --> 00:30:44.660
Also, the androids' mother is able to have babies.
这非常离奇，珍娜。

741
00:30:44.840 --> 00:30:46.420
It's very bizarre, Jenna.
太离奇了。

742
00:30:46.600 --> 00:30:47.560
It's so bizarre.
我居然在看《哈利法克斯探戈》而不是《异星灾变》，这对我来说一点也不奇怪。

743
00:30:47.560 --> 00:30:54.960
It is not a surprise to me that I'm watching Last Tango in Halifax instead of Raised by Wolves.
听着，《哈利法克斯探戈》正合我胃口。

744
00:30:54.980 --> 00:30:58.120
Now listen, Last Tango in Halifax is right up my alley.
你知道我喜欢任何BBC制作的节目，但我也很喜欢那种奇怪的科幻片。

745
00:30:58.300 --> 00:31:03.540
You know I love any kind of like BBC programming, but I also love me some weird sci-fi.
好吧，我给你展示一下。

746
00:31:03.720 --> 00:31:04.660
Okay, I'm going to show you.
这是德怀特在《第二人生》里的飞行方式，这是“母亲”的飞行方式。

747
00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:09.700
This is how Dwight flies in Simple Life, and this is how Mother flies.
嗯哼。

748
00:31:10.120 --> 00:31:10.480
Mm-hmm.
我看到了。

749
00:31:10.680 --> 00:31:11.360
I see it.
他们都是直立着身体，双臂张开。

750
00:31:11.480 --> 00:31:13.920
They both go upright with their arms out.
没错。

751
00:31:14.160 --> 00:31:15.420
It's very creepy.
这太诡异了。

752
00:31:15.940 --> 00:31:16.620
I know.
我知道。

753
00:31:16.620 --> 00:31:20.560
Anyone else that watch Raised by Wolves, go to 3 minutes, 39 seconds.
还有谁在看《异星灾变》的，去看看3分39秒处。

754
00:31:20.820 --> 00:31:24.300
Watch how Dwight does his liftoff, and it will remind you of Mother.
看看德怀特是怎么起飞的，会让你想起“母亲”。

755
00:31:24.620 --> 00:31:26.400
Angela will also put that on the pod.
安吉拉也会把它发到播客上。

756
00:31:26.900 --> 00:31:28.100
I'm going to put it in our stories.
我会把它发到我们的快拍里。

757
00:31:28.460 --> 00:31:30.820
I looked up Dwight's profile on Second Life.
我查了德怀特在《第二人生》里的个人资料。

758
00:31:31.020 --> 00:31:31.480
You did?
你查了？

759
00:31:31.740 --> 00:31:32.280
I did.
我查了。

760
00:31:32.420 --> 00:31:33.100
It's still there.
它还在那儿。

761
00:31:33.240 --> 00:31:35.380
Here's what he has down as his interests.
这是他填写的兴趣爱好。

762
00:31:49.840 --> 00:31:58.400
His talents are listed as avid Cornhusk Dollmaker, Beat Sculptor, and Not-Tying Champion.
他的才艺写着：狂热的玉米皮玩偶制作师、节拍雕塑家和打结冠军。

763
00:31:58.400 --> 00:32:07.520
He had to list a goal for his Second Life, and he wrote to calculate the exchange between shroot bucks and Linden dollars.
他必须为他的《第二人生》写下一个目标，他写的是计算“施鲁特币”和“林登币”之间的汇率。

764
00:32:07.520 --> 00:32:10.880
Linden dollars are the currency in Second Life.
林登币是《第二人生》里的货币。

765
00:32:11.280 --> 00:32:11.560
Okay.
好吧。

766
00:32:12.020 --> 00:32:12.980
So there you have it.
所以就是这样。

767
00:32:13.080 --> 00:32:20.500
When he's not flying like Mother, he is trying to calculate the exchange between shroot bucks and Linden dollars.
当他不学“母亲”飞行的时候，他就在研究怎么计算施鲁特币和林登币的汇率。

768
00:32:20.760 --> 00:32:21.620
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

769
00:32:21.620 --> 00:32:26.500
Up next, Michael is going to pitch his big idea to the ad guys.
接下来，迈克尔要向广告商推销他的宏大创意。

770
00:32:26.760 --> 00:32:33.180
I want you guys to know a deleted scene would have come before this between Jim and Michael that is so delicious and fun.
我想让你们知道，在这之前本来有一段吉姆和迈克尔的删减片段，非常精彩有趣。

771
00:32:33.420 --> 00:32:36.320
Basically, Michael wants to practice pitch to Jim.
基本上，迈克尔想找吉姆练习推销。

772
00:32:36.580 --> 00:32:38.520
He brings Jim in the office, right?
他把吉姆叫进办公室，对吧？

773
00:32:38.680 --> 00:32:45.280
He has Jim sit behind his desk so he can practice pitch, and he says, this is his pitch to Jim.
他让吉姆坐在他的办公桌后，好让他练习推销，他说，这是他给吉姆的推销方案。

774
00:32:45.420 --> 00:32:47.120
We start on a blank piece of paper.
画面从一张白纸开始。

775
00:32:47.300 --> 00:32:50.240
We widen to reveal ancient Rome.
镜头拉远，显露出古罗马。

776
00:32:50.240 --> 00:32:52.140
Jim's like, can't do that.
吉姆说，这不行。

777
00:32:52.640 --> 00:32:53.440
Michael's like, okay.
迈克尔说，好吧。

778
00:32:53.860 --> 00:32:58.200
We widen to reveal a spaceship blasting out of a woman's womb.
镜头拉远，显露出一艘从女人的子宫里发射出来的宇宙飞船。

779
00:32:58.720 --> 00:32:58.900
What?
什么？

780
00:32:59.420 --> 00:33:03.000
Then they do this very funny role play where Jim's like, get out of my office.
然后他们演了一段非常搞笑的角色扮演，吉姆说，滚出我的办公室。

781
00:33:03.120 --> 00:33:04.500
It's like becomes a whole thing.
这简直闹成了一团。

782
00:33:04.700 --> 00:33:10.440
But for real, the pitch Michael settles on is this one, and I thought we had to hear it.
但说真的，迈克尔最终确定的推销方案是这个，我觉得我们必须听听看。

783
00:33:10.620 --> 00:33:11.860
Sam, can you play it?
萨姆，能播放一下吗？

784
00:33:12.140 --> 00:33:15.820
Little girl in a field holding a flower.
一个小女孩在田野里拿着一朵花。

785
00:33:16.060 --> 00:33:19.460
We zoom back to find that she's in the desert.
我们拉远镜头，发现她身处沙漠之中。

786
00:33:20.240 --> 00:33:21.960
And the field is an oasis.
而那片田野是一片绿洲。

787
00:33:22.340 --> 00:33:23.480
We zoom back further.
我们继续拉远镜头。

788
00:33:24.440 --> 00:33:29.040
The desert is a sandbox in the world's largest resort hotel.
沙漠是世界上最大的度假酒店里的一个沙坑。

789
00:33:29.320 --> 00:33:30.420
Zoom back further.
再拉远一点。

790
00:33:30.740 --> 00:33:36.800
The hotel is actually the playground of the world's largest prison.
酒店其实是世界上最大的监狱的游乐场。

791
00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:38.840
But we zoom back further.
但我们继续拉远镜头。

792
00:33:39.140 --> 00:33:40.920
I can tell that your time is valuable.
我看得出你的时间很宝贵。

793
00:33:41.060 --> 00:33:45.840
Oh, well, I love what he says when the guy is like, listen, I can tell your time is valuable.
噢，我太喜欢当那个人说“听着，我看得出你的时间很宝贵”时，迈克尔的回答了。

794
00:33:45.960 --> 00:33:49.220
And Michael's like, well, actually, I don't get paid by the hour anymore.
迈克尔说，嗯，其实我现在不是按小时计费的。

795
00:33:49.400 --> 00:33:50.560
I get paid by the year.
我是按年计费的。

796
00:33:50.820 --> 00:33:53.640
So, basically, I can waste as much time as I want.
所以，基本上，我可以随心所欲地浪费时间。

797
00:33:54.020 --> 00:33:54.800
Not a problem.
没问题。

798
00:33:54.800 --> 00:33:58.540
Yes, but I love that this is the pitch that he led with.
是的，但我很喜欢他最终选用了这个推销方案。

799
00:33:58.720 --> 00:34:02.560
And knowing that he had other ideas, but this is what he went with.
而且要知道他还有其他点子，但他最终选了这个。

800
00:34:02.860 --> 00:34:04.300
The ad guys are great.
那些广告商太棒了。

801
00:34:04.440 --> 00:34:06.900
They're so real in how they react to Michael.
他们对迈克尔的反应非常真实。

802
00:34:07.140 --> 00:34:10.580
They say, listen, we made something for the Nashua branch.
他们说，听着，我们为纳舒厄分公司制作了一些东西。

803
00:34:10.740 --> 00:34:12.080
Why don't we show that to you?
我们要不要给你们看看？

804
00:34:12.240 --> 00:34:14.480
And it'll give you an idea of what we can do.
这能让你们了解我们能做到什么程度。

805
00:34:15.100 --> 00:34:16.840
So, he plays this commercial.
于是，他播放了这个广告。

806
00:34:17.360 --> 00:34:23.160
And then they explain the only part of the commercial they're allowed to alter is the last five seconds.
然后他们解释说，广告中唯一允许他们修改的部分就是最后五秒。

807
00:34:23.460 --> 00:34:23.620
Yeah.
是啊。

808
00:34:23.700 --> 00:34:24.360
And Michael's like, what?
迈克尔就说，什么？

809
00:34:24.360 --> 00:34:25.560
We just wave at the end?
我们最后只能挥挥手？

810
00:34:25.720 --> 00:34:27.380
He goes, you know, you could clap.
他说，你知道，你们可以鼓掌。

811
00:34:27.520 --> 00:34:28.460
You know, make it your own.
你知道，发挥你们的创意。

812
00:34:28.620 --> 00:34:28.760
Yeah.
是啊。

813
00:34:28.840 --> 00:34:30.660
This is where you can really get creative.
这就是你们真正可以发挥创意的地方。

814
00:34:31.040 --> 00:34:32.280
You can be inside.
你们可以在室内。

815
00:34:32.280 --> 00:34:33.300
You can be outside.
你们可以在室外。

816
00:34:33.660 --> 00:34:35.080
We had a fan question.
我们有一个粉丝提问。

817
00:34:35.460 --> 00:34:43.760
Aaron Jassa, Harry Driscoll, Molly Coates, and many others, they wanted to know who directed this commercial that plays in the middle of the episode.
亚伦·贾萨、哈里·德里斯科尔、莫莉·科茨以及许多其他人，他们想知道是谁执导了这一集中间播放的那个广告。

818
00:34:43.760 --> 00:34:45.160
Was it Jason Reitman?
是杰森·雷特曼吗？

819
00:34:45.400 --> 00:34:47.460
Yes, it was Jason Reitman.
是的，确实是杰森·雷特曼。

820
00:34:47.740 --> 00:34:55.620
I texted with BJ about this commercial, and he told me that Jason Reitman had directed real commercials before this.
我曾就这个广告和BJ发过短信，他告诉我杰森·雷特曼在拍这个之前就执导过真正的商业广告。

821
00:34:55.760 --> 00:35:04.920
And he remembers that it was so cool because Jason laid out this big circular track on the floor and had the camera going around in circles.
他记得当时非常酷，因为杰森在地板上铺了一个巨大的圆形轨道，让摄像机绕着圈拍。

822
00:35:05.100 --> 00:35:08.420
And BJ was like, I had never seen anything like that before.
BJ当时就觉得，我以前从没见过那样的东西。

823
00:35:08.640 --> 00:35:09.580
It was so cool.
太酷了。

824
00:35:09.580 --> 00:35:14.660
Well, we asked Jason about filming this fake commercial, and here's what he had to say.
好吧，我们问了杰森关于拍摄这个虚假广告的事，以下是他的回答。

825
00:35:15.320 --> 00:35:19.820
The episode Local Ad contained two commercials inside it, and I had been a commercial director.
《本地广告》那一集里包含了两个广告，而我曾经是一名商业广告导演。

826
00:35:19.960 --> 00:35:21.740
I was a bad commercial director, I should say.
我应该说，我是一名糟糕的商业广告导演。

827
00:35:21.940 --> 00:35:27.600
You know, the majority of the commercials that I directed were ones that if you saw, you would revoke my Director's Guild card.
你知道，我执导的大部分广告，如果你看了，你都会吊销我的导演工会会员证。

828
00:35:27.600 --> 00:35:29.180
You would just say, you're not allowed to direct again.
你会直接说，你不准再执导了。

829
00:35:29.320 --> 00:35:32.820
And then I would, you know, name clients, but that would be rude.
然后我会，你知道，列举客户，但这会很不礼貌。

830
00:35:33.040 --> 00:35:39.200
But, you know, typical fast food and beer and just, but like, not good work.
但是，你知道，就是典型的快餐和啤酒广告，总之，不是什么好作品。

831
00:35:39.200 --> 00:35:42.260
I was not Spike Jonze, but I learned that format.
我不是斯派克·琼斯，但我学会了那种格式。

832
00:35:42.700 --> 00:35:46.000
There's certain things that you may not know how to do authentically, but you know how to satirize.
有些事情你可能不知道如何做得地道，但你知道如何去讽刺。

833
00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:55.380
Like, I know that I could never direct a David Fincher film, but I love him so much as a filmmaker that I could probably direct a satire of a David Fincher film.
就像我知道我永远无法执导大卫·芬奇的电影，但我非常喜欢他这位电影制作人，所以我大概能执导一部讽刺大卫·芬奇电影的作品。

834
00:35:55.500 --> 00:36:00.200
And so, I don't know how to direct a great commercial, but I think I know how to direct the satire of a good commercial.
所以，我不知道如何执导一个伟大的商业广告，但我认为我知道如何执导一个优秀商业广告的讽刺版。

835
00:36:00.360 --> 00:36:06.900
And that was the kind of the great thing about doing the Dunder Mifflin ad, was I felt my commercial brain trying to do the best,
这就是制作邓德·米夫林广告最棒的地方，我感觉我的商业大脑试图做出最好、

836
00:36:07.040 --> 00:36:12.120
worst version of what Dunder Mifflin would hand Michael Scott, which was this kind of cutesy commercial.
最烂的版本，也就是邓德·米夫林会交给迈克尔·斯科特的那种矫揉造作的广告。

837
00:36:12.120 --> 00:36:15.880
It starred Jeff Witzke, who is an actor I've worked with since I was a kid.
它由杰夫·维茨克主演，他是我从小就合作过的演员。

838
00:36:15.980 --> 00:36:19.000
He literally was in my first short film and has been in everything I've ever made since.
他确实出演了我的第一部短片，从那以后我制作的每一部作品里都有他。

839
00:36:19.100 --> 00:36:20.660
And he was the star of it, and that was great.
他是主角，这太棒了。

840
00:36:21.560 --> 00:36:25.560
I love that Jason just uses his friend Jeff in everything.
我喜欢杰森在所有作品里都用他的朋友杰夫这一点。

841
00:36:25.840 --> 00:36:26.940
I just think that's wonderful.
我觉得这太美妙了。

842
00:36:27.240 --> 00:36:29.700
Jenna, I want you to be in everything I do from here on out.
珍娜，我希望从今往后我做的每一件事里都有你。

843
00:36:30.360 --> 00:36:30.800
Great.
太好了。

844
00:36:31.400 --> 00:36:32.300
I love it.
我喜欢。

845
00:36:32.600 --> 00:36:32.900
Okay.
好的。

846
00:36:33.680 --> 00:36:36.300
Well, we have some crossover connections with Jeff.
嗯，我们和杰夫之间还有一些交叉联系。

847
00:36:36.460 --> 00:36:37.120
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

848
00:36:37.120 --> 00:36:43.940
He was also in Mindy and Brenda, the TV short written by Mindy Kaling and Brenda Withers.
他也出演了《明迪和布伦达》，那部由明迪·卡灵和布伦达·威瑟斯编剧的电视短片。

849
00:36:44.220 --> 00:36:44.780
Oh.
哦。

850
00:36:45.020 --> 00:36:45.300
Yeah.
是啊。

851
00:36:45.480 --> 00:36:46.960
He played the sales clerk.
他演的是售货员。

852
00:36:47.340 --> 00:36:49.140
Well, lady, guess what?
好吧，女士，你猜怎么着？

853
00:36:50.060 --> 00:36:52.300
He also did a guest spot on Monk.
他还客串过《神探阿蒙》。

854
00:36:52.420 --> 00:36:56.280
He played Human Cannonball in Mr. Monk Goes to the Circus.
他在《阿蒙去马戏团》那一集里演了“人体炮弹”。

855
00:36:56.560 --> 00:36:57.700
That one really got me.
那集真的戳中我了。

856
00:36:57.860 --> 00:36:59.480
I might need to look that one up.
我可能得去查查那一集。

857
00:36:59.640 --> 00:37:00.560
Human Cannonball.
人体炮弹。

858
00:37:00.760 --> 00:37:01.380
Very curious.
真好奇。

859
00:37:01.680 --> 00:37:04.000
You might need to see what the Human Cannonball looks like.
你可能得去看看“人体炮弹”长什么样。

860
00:37:04.180 --> 00:37:04.600
Yes.
没错。

861
00:37:04.600 --> 00:37:10.060
So not only did Jason hire Jeff again, he also hired a friend that he had worked with
所以杰森不仅再次聘用了杰夫，还聘请了一位他以前合作过的朋友

862
00:37:10.060 --> 00:37:12.180
before to compose that music.
来创作那段音乐。

863
00:37:12.180 --> 00:37:16.020
That sort of like, I don't know, it's like salsa music that's playing in the background.
那听起来有点像，我不知道，就像背景里放的萨尔萨舞曲。

864
00:37:16.020 --> 00:37:22.600
It was composed by the same composer that did all the music for Juno, Matteo Messina.
那是马泰奥·梅西纳创作的，他也是《朱诺》所有配乐的作曲家。

865
00:37:22.860 --> 00:37:24.080
I love that.
我太喜欢那个了。

866
00:37:24.900 --> 00:37:27.180
Now things are going to get awkward.
现在事情要变得尴尬了。

867
00:37:27.660 --> 00:37:33.300
Andy pulls Dwight aside to get advice on how to get to first base with Angela.
安迪把德怀特拉到一边，想请教如何跟安吉拉有进一步的发展。

868
00:37:33.300 --> 00:37:38.700
He says they've been necking a lot, but that means that they are literally rubbing their
他说他们一直在“脖子贴脖子”，但那意味着他们真的只是在

869
00:37:38.700 --> 00:37:39.460
necks together.
互相蹭脖子。

870
00:37:39.740 --> 00:37:41.120
There's no kissing involved.
根本没有接吻。

871
00:37:41.320 --> 00:37:43.240
Why don't we have any footage of that?
为什么我们没有那段录像？

872
00:37:44.020 --> 00:37:45.420
I don't know.
我不知道。

873
00:37:45.860 --> 00:37:47.080
I don't know.
我不知道。

874
00:37:47.260 --> 00:37:50.200
Angela, we had a fan question from Amy Noki.
安吉拉，我们收到一个粉丝艾米·诺基的提问。

875
00:37:50.640 --> 00:37:55.440
She's dying to know, what is your backstory for Angela and Andy?
她特别想知道，你对安吉拉和安迪这段感情的背景设定是什么？

876
00:37:55.580 --> 00:37:57.080
And what is with the necking?
还有那个“脖子贴脖子”是怎么回事？

877
00:37:57.080 --> 00:38:02.100
Do you think this was standard for Angela, or is it because she can't stomach Andy and
你觉得这对安吉拉来说是常态，还是因为她受不了安迪，

878
00:38:02.100 --> 00:38:04.140
she's just trying to get back at Dwight?
只是想以此报复德怀特？

879
00:38:04.340 --> 00:38:05.540
I love this question.
我喜欢这个问题。

880
00:38:05.740 --> 00:38:10.080
I thought that Angela went out with Andy as sort of a revenge date.
我觉得安吉拉跟安迪约会算是一种报复性约会。

881
00:38:10.340 --> 00:38:12.000
She was very mad at Dwight.
她当时非常生德怀特的气。

882
00:38:12.200 --> 00:38:14.140
She really thought she was done with Dwight.
她真的以为自己和德怀特彻底完了。

883
00:38:14.260 --> 00:38:15.940
She was super, super angry with him.
她对他感到非常、非常愤怒。

884
00:38:16.040 --> 00:38:21.340
And as she started dating Andy, I think it became very clear to her that really Dwight had her
当她开始和安迪约会时，我觉得她很清楚，其实德怀特才拥有

885
00:38:21.340 --> 00:38:24.220
heart, but she was too prideful to admit that.
她的心，但她太骄傲了，不肯承认。

886
00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:28.260
So she tried to date Andy, but it was a chore.
所以她试着和安迪约会，但这成了一种苦差事。

887
00:38:28.540 --> 00:38:32.840
And I think the necking thing is just something she was doing to put him off.
我觉得“脖子贴脖子”只是她为了敷衍他而做的事。

888
00:38:33.040 --> 00:38:36.620
Like, how can I let him touch me, but not really touch me?
就像是，我该怎么让他碰我，但又不是真的碰我呢？

889
00:38:36.980 --> 00:38:40.300
So yeah, I think her heart wasn't in it from the beginning.
所以没错，我觉得她从一开始就没走心。

890
00:38:40.960 --> 00:38:42.620
Yeah, I was thinking about it.
是啊，我当时也在想这个问题。

891
00:38:42.620 --> 00:38:50.400
And, you know, Angela can be very fussy and very structured, but we saw her going at it
而且，你知道，安吉拉平时非常挑剔、非常有条理，但我们见过她在

892
00:38:50.400 --> 00:38:55.040
in Jim's little toy playhouse thing and email surveillance.
吉姆的玩具屋里和邮件监控那集里的表现。

893
00:38:55.040 --> 00:39:00.660
So when she's into someone, it's not like she puts people through these weird paces of
所以当她真心喜欢某人时，她并不会让人经历那些奇怪的步骤，

894
00:39:00.660 --> 00:39:02.880
like, okay, first we just rub our necks together.
比如，好吧，我们先蹭蹭脖子。

895
00:39:03.080 --> 00:39:05.220
I think this was exclusive to Andy.
我觉得这只是针对安迪的特殊待遇。

896
00:39:05.480 --> 00:39:05.940
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

897
00:39:06.220 --> 00:39:06.400
Yeah.
是啊。

898
00:39:06.600 --> 00:39:08.040
And maybe the senator too.
也许对参议员也是这样。

899
00:39:08.340 --> 00:39:08.680
Perhaps.
或许吧。

900
00:39:08.800 --> 00:39:10.860
I really think Dwight was the love of her life.
我真的觉得德怀特才是她一生挚爱。

901
00:39:10.860 --> 00:39:13.520
And, you know, it just took them a while to get there.
而且，你知道，他们花了一段时间才达成共识。

902
00:39:13.720 --> 00:39:14.560
Poor Dwight.
可怜的德怀特。

903
00:39:14.880 --> 00:39:16.780
He's having to listen to all this.
他不得不听这些话。

904
00:39:17.060 --> 00:39:19.200
And he tries to put Andy off.
他试图劝阻安迪。

905
00:39:19.360 --> 00:39:21.360
He says, I don't think we should talk about this.
他说，我觉得我们不该谈论这个。

906
00:39:21.500 --> 00:39:22.820
People might overhear us.
别人可能会偷听到。

907
00:39:22.980 --> 00:39:27.440
But then Andy just takes that to mean that they should come up with code names.
但安迪却以为他的意思是他们该起些代号。

908
00:39:28.460 --> 00:39:33.340
Dwight's like, okay, well, Angela can stay the same, but let's change Andy to Dwight.
德怀特说，好吧，安吉拉的名字可以保留，但把安迪改成德怀特。

909
00:39:33.740 --> 00:39:34.120
Hmm.
嗯。

910
00:39:34.640 --> 00:39:34.960
Okay.
好吧。

911
00:39:35.280 --> 00:39:35.500
Yeah.
是啊。

912
00:39:35.640 --> 00:39:39.040
And Andy's like, that's not really, that's not how this works.
安迪说，那不太对，事情不是这么运作的。

913
00:39:39.040 --> 00:39:46.860
Lady, this really reminded me of how you and I tried to come up with code names when we
女士，这真的让我想起你我以前试图起代号的时候，

914
00:39:46.860 --> 00:39:50.960
would have conversations and we were afraid other people could overhear us.
当时我们谈话时总担心别人会偷听。

915
00:39:51.380 --> 00:39:54.240
And our code names were about this good.
我们的代号也就这种水平。

916
00:39:54.440 --> 00:39:56.080
They were so obvious.
太显眼了。

917
00:39:56.080 --> 00:39:58.540
It would be like a person's initials.
就像是用名字的首字母缩写一样。

918
00:39:58.600 --> 00:39:59.780
So obvious.
太明显了。

919
00:40:00.160 --> 00:40:00.780
I know.
我知道。

920
00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:03.020
We're not going to be spies, Jenna.
我们当不了间谍，珍娜。

921
00:40:03.460 --> 00:40:08.100
We're not going to be spies, but we're going to be mom detectives solving small crimes.
我们当不了间谍，但我们可以当那种侦破社区小案子的妈妈侦探。

922
00:40:08.100 --> 00:40:10.600
I would love to be a mom detective with you.
我很乐意和你一起当妈妈侦探。

923
00:40:10.900 --> 00:40:15.720
Mom detectives solving the small crimes no one cares about in your neighborhood.
妈妈侦探，专门侦破社区里没人关心的那些小案子。

924
00:40:17.040 --> 00:40:18.360
It's a hit.
这绝对会火。

925
00:40:18.640 --> 00:40:22.220
Who graffitied the construction cone at the intersection?
是谁在十字路口的施工锥上乱涂乱画的？

926
00:40:23.100 --> 00:40:23.660
Exactly.
没错。

927
00:40:24.140 --> 00:40:25.320
We'll find out.
我们会查出来的。

928
00:40:25.620 --> 00:40:26.700
We'll tell you.
我们会告诉你的。

929
00:40:26.880 --> 00:40:27.620
We're on it.
我们正在调查。

930
00:40:27.920 --> 00:40:32.180
So coming up, we have a scene between Ryan and Michael that is so funny to me.
接下来，我们要聊聊瑞安和迈克尔之间的一场戏，我觉得特别好笑。

931
00:40:32.880 --> 00:40:37.600
When Michael calls him, you know, to gripe, first of all, he calls him Rye.
迈克尔打电话去抱怨时，首先，他叫他“小黑麦”。

932
00:40:39.400 --> 00:40:41.460
Ryan is like, don't call me about small probleMs.
瑞安说，别为了小问题给我打电话。

933
00:40:41.600 --> 00:40:42.780
What have I told you about that?
我跟你说过多少次了？

934
00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:43.580
Yeah.
是啊。

935
00:40:43.660 --> 00:40:46.240
And he says, well, you don't like it when I call you about big problems either.
他说，好吧，反正我打给你说大问题你也不高兴。

936
00:40:46.520 --> 00:40:47.580
So what do you want from me?
那你到底想让我怎么样？

937
00:40:47.620 --> 00:40:48.240
What do you want?
你到底想要什么？

938
00:40:48.460 --> 00:40:52.740
So Jason said on the DVD commentary that they shot this in real time.
杰森在DVD评论音轨里说，他们是实时拍摄这场戏的。

939
00:40:53.140 --> 00:40:57.940
